1
00:00:03,134 --> 00:00:07,694
I see blue, I see blue

2
00:00:07,804 --> 00:00:12,674
Looking up at the big, clear sky

3
00:00:12,774 --> 00:00:17,714
As I feel, as I feel

4
00:00:18,084 --> 00:00:23,154
Fresh cut grass right here where I lie

5
00:00:23,154 --> 00:00:28,094
Playing a fun game of hide-and-seek

6
00:00:28,094 --> 00:00:32,794
From the sunflower field, take a peek

7
00:00:33,124 --> 00:00:37,934
Then we'll blow, then we'll blow

8
00:00:37,934 --> 00:00:42,834
Round, round soap bubbles, you and I

9
00:00:49,644 --> 00:00:52,784
Kobato.

10
00:00:52,784 --> 00:00:55,614
Kobato.
Dou sureba iin dakke?

11
00:00:55,614 --> 00:01:00,024
Kobato.
Atarimae no kototte itsumo

12
00:01:00,924 --> 00:01:04,224
Muzukashii na

13
00:01:04,224 --> 00:01:06,994
Ureshii toki waratte

14
00:01:06,994 --> 00:01:11,294
Suki na toki ni utaitai dake

15
00:01:11,864 --> 00:01:14,304
Na no ni

16
00:01:15,604 --> 00:01:19,974
Itsuka negai wa kanau to

17
00:01:20,414 --> 00:01:23,684
Demo "itsuka" tte dore kurai?

18
00:01:23,684 --> 00:01:27,174
Machikirenai yo

19
00:01:27,314 --> 00:01:33,084
123! no aizu de ryoute hirogete

20
00:01:33,084 --> 00:01:38,294
Zenshin ni hikari wo atsumete

21
00:01:38,294 --> 00:01:41,134
Doko ni aru no?

22
00:01:41,134 --> 00:01:44,464
Oshiete, watashi ni dekiru koto

23
00:01:44,464 --> 00:01:47,304
Meippai kizu tsuite

24
00:01:47,304 --> 00:01:50,204
Seiippai hashitte

25
00:01:50,204 --> 00:01:54,174
Nan juu kai koronde naite

26
00:01:54,174 --> 00:01:57,214
Sore de mo mada

27
00:01:57,214 --> 00:02:01,244
Akireru kurai

28
00:02:01,714 --> 00:02:05,884
Ashita wo shinjiteru

29
00:02:15,094 --> 00:02:16,164
I see white, I see white

30
00:02:16,164 --> 00:02:20,234
...The Boy's Organ Days.
I see white, I see white

31
00:02:20,234 --> 00:02:22,134
...The Boy's Organ Days.
Chasing clouds as they drift away

32
00:02:22,134 --> 00:02:24,604
Chasing clouds as they drift away

33
00:02:24,604 --> 00:02:25,594
And there!

34
00:02:26,914 --> 00:02:31,414
Let's all run, let's all run

35
00:02:31,414 --> 00:02:31,644
Me and my friends, 'cause we love to play

36
00:02:31,644 --> 00:02:35,284
You've got a lot of energy first thing in the
morning in this darn hot weather!
Me and my friends, 'cause we love to play

37
00:02:35,284 --> 00:02:36,614
What is that song?
Me and my friends, 'cause we love to play

38
00:02:36,614 --> 00:02:36,684
What is that song?

39
00:02:36,684 --> 00:02:41,644
I learned it from the children at Yomogi
Kindergarten. Isn't it a fun song?

40
00:02:42,824 --> 00:02:45,724
When we get to the...

41
00:02:45,724 --> 00:02:46,664
Huh?

42
00:03:02,614 --> 00:03:04,484
That was frightening!

43
00:03:04,484 --> 00:03:06,744
I thought I was going to fall.

44
00:03:06,744 --> 00:03:07,974
Would you be quiet?!

45
00:03:09,714 --> 00:03:11,774
Oh! Good morning!

46
00:03:11,924 --> 00:03:14,684
It's Sunday morning.
What the heck are you doing?

47
00:03:15,254 --> 00:03:18,854
I-I'm hanging out the bedding to air.
It's such a beautiful day.

48
00:03:21,894 --> 00:03:25,064
Man, can't you do anything
without causing a major stir?

49
00:03:27,434 --> 00:03:28,574
He's not nice.

50
00:03:28,574 --> 00:03:32,804
Dobato...

51
00:03:32,804 --> 00:03:34,114
Ioryogi-san!

52
00:03:34,114 --> 00:03:35,634
Are you okay?

53
00:03:35,944 --> 00:03:37,504
Do I look okay?

54
00:03:37,844 --> 00:03:38,844
No I'm not!

55
00:03:38,844 --> 00:03:42,254
Like I keep telling you, in this
world I am a stuffed doll!

56
00:03:42,254 --> 00:03:43,414
Don't expect miracles!

57
00:03:43,414 --> 00:03:45,474
I'm sorry.

58
00:03:45,954 --> 00:03:47,014
See you later.

59
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:50,224
Take care, now. Have a nice day.

60
00:03:50,324 --> 00:03:51,414
Yes, ma'am.

61
00:03:52,394 --> 00:03:55,794
The guy Ms. Chitose is seeing off.
That's Fujimoto, isn't it?

62
00:03:56,134 --> 00:03:57,624
I think that's pretty obvious.

63
00:03:58,264 --> 00:03:59,334
It's strange.

64
00:03:59,334 --> 00:04:00,274
What is?

65
00:04:00,274 --> 00:04:04,704
Fujimoto was just in the next room,
and now he's already out the front door.

66
00:04:04,704 --> 00:04:06,734
He sure is a busy man.

67
00:04:07,974 --> 00:04:09,344
Maybe...

68
00:04:10,744 --> 00:04:13,644
Maybe there are two Fujimoto's.

69
00:04:14,884 --> 00:04:18,254
It's not like we're in a suspense movie!

70
00:04:23,394 --> 00:04:25,694
Kobato, what was that noise?

71
00:04:25,864 --> 00:04:27,834
Oh, oh, nothing!

72
00:04:33,304 --> 00:04:34,564
Where are you going?

73
00:04:34,704 --> 00:04:36,474
Yomogi Kindergarten.

74
00:04:36,474 --> 00:04:37,774
It's closed today.

75
00:04:37,774 --> 00:04:40,804
It's a nice day. I thought I'd go
and hang out the futons.

76
00:04:40,874 --> 00:04:43,714
Hey Kobato. Do you know what you're doing?

77
00:04:44,484 --> 00:04:45,774
What do you mean?

78
00:04:45,984 --> 00:04:48,244
What is your purpose in coming here?

79
00:04:48,454 --> 00:04:51,784
To fill the bottle with kompeito.

80
00:04:51,784 --> 00:04:57,424
Well if you know that, don't you think there are
other things you could be doing on a Sunday?

81
00:04:58,664 --> 00:04:59,994
But...

82
00:05:07,874 --> 00:05:12,864
Right now, I just want to do what I
can to help Yomogi Kindergarten.

83
00:05:14,914 --> 00:05:17,714
I report! Regarding Yomogi Kindergarten!

84
00:05:17,714 --> 00:05:21,044
The former principal was apparently
tricked into borrowing money!

85
00:05:21,714 --> 00:05:23,154
Former principal?

86
00:05:23,384 --> 00:05:28,944
Yes. Sayaka Okiura's father.
He died two years ago.

87
00:05:29,454 --> 00:05:32,084
Looks like a real bad bunch who tricked him.

88
00:05:32,194 --> 00:05:36,724
Not only that, one of them seems to
be a relative of Sayaka Okiura.

89
00:05:55,214 --> 00:05:56,704
Ms. Sayaka.

90
00:05:57,824 --> 00:05:59,414
Kobato?

91
00:06:01,394 --> 00:06:02,484
What's the matter?

92
00:06:02,894 --> 00:06:04,154
Today's a holiday.

93
00:06:04,424 --> 00:06:05,364
Yes.

94
00:06:05,364 --> 00:06:07,724
I came to air out everybody's futons.

95
00:06:08,634 --> 00:06:09,924
Futons?

96
00:06:10,194 --> 00:06:13,064
Yes. It's such a nice day.

97
00:06:23,214 --> 00:06:25,334
It sure is a nice day.

98
00:06:26,144 --> 00:06:28,514
I didn't even notice.

99
00:06:30,254 --> 00:06:33,184
Okay. Let's hang them out together.

100
00:06:33,854 --> 00:06:34,984
Yes!

101
00:06:36,694 --> 00:06:43,324
Chisato's really happy. She says she's glad
that a nice girl like you has moved in.

102
00:06:43,394 --> 00:06:48,594
I enjoy living there. Ms. Chisato and Chiho
and Chise are so much fun to be with.

103
00:06:49,574 --> 00:06:51,194
How about Fujimoto, next door?

104
00:06:52,904 --> 00:06:55,104
Has he been mean to you?

105
00:06:56,174 --> 00:07:03,214
Well sometimes he's mean and then
sometimes he isn't. I don't know.

106
00:07:03,924 --> 00:07:05,784
I don't understand him.

107
00:07:07,824 --> 00:07:10,914
It many not seem like it,
but Fujimoto is a kind person.

108
00:07:12,094 --> 00:07:14,124
He's been that way since he was a small child.

109
00:07:16,694 --> 00:07:18,564
Fujimoto as a small child?

110
00:07:18,564 --> 00:07:20,334
That's hard to imagine.

111
00:07:20,604 --> 00:07:21,864
Want to see a picture?

112
00:07:28,514 --> 00:07:31,134
Sorry to keep you waiting. Here it is.

113
00:07:32,314 --> 00:07:33,414
Look.

114
00:07:33,414 --> 00:07:35,854
Wow! He's tiny.

115
00:07:35,854 --> 00:07:37,824
This is Fujimoto?

116
00:07:38,054 --> 00:07:42,584
Yes. We took this picture the first
day he arrived here.

117
00:07:42,924 --> 00:07:46,954
Fujimoto was a Yomogi Kindergarten student?

118
00:07:48,194 --> 00:07:49,564
No, no he wasn't.

119
00:07:52,864 --> 00:07:55,964
Fujimoto was an orphan.

120
00:07:56,034 --> 00:07:57,364
Orphan?

121
00:07:57,844 --> 00:07:59,674
What's an orphan?

122
00:07:59,674 --> 00:08:05,114
Oh um... An orphan is a child who doesn't
have a mother or a father or a home.

123
00:08:05,114 --> 00:08:06,084
Huh?

124
00:08:06,584 --> 00:08:09,914
If you don't intend to care for her
to the end, don't get involved.

125
00:08:10,524 --> 00:08:13,824
If you're only taking care of it
half-heartedly to satisfy yourself,

126
00:08:13,824 --> 00:08:15,624
you're just as guilty as the
people who abandoned it.

127
00:08:16,824 --> 00:08:18,084
That's why...

128
00:08:18,364 --> 00:08:20,294
He said those things.

129
00:08:20,994 --> 00:08:22,124
Kobato?

130
00:08:22,734 --> 00:08:27,224
Please tell me more. I'd like to know
more about Fujimoto's childhood.

131
00:08:32,604 --> 00:08:33,764
All right.

132
00:08:35,344 --> 00:08:37,814
That was about fourteen years ago.

133
00:08:38,284 --> 00:08:41,584
My father took Fujimoto in.

134
00:08:43,584 --> 00:08:45,144
I'm home, Sayaka.

135
00:08:45,624 --> 00:08:49,214
This is Kiyokazu Fujimoto,
the boy I was telling you about.

136
00:08:50,894 --> 00:08:53,794
Fujimoto, this is my daughter Sayaka.

137
00:08:54,234 --> 00:08:57,024
Hi, I'm Sayaka. Nice to meet you Fujimoto.

138
00:09:02,334 --> 00:09:05,944
I know! A picture! We need a picture
to mark this moment! Right?

139
00:09:05,944 --> 00:09:07,674
I'll go and get the camera right away.

140
00:09:07,774 --> 00:09:09,974
Where'd I put that camera?

141
00:09:14,454 --> 00:09:16,044
Are you ready?

142
00:09:17,014 --> 00:09:21,014
Everybody say "Yomo-giii."

143
00:09:23,154 --> 00:09:27,284
And from that day on, Fujimoto was to live here.

144
00:09:27,494 --> 00:09:30,264
Fujimoto looks angry.

145
00:09:30,504 --> 00:09:34,934
Yeah maybe. When he first arrived,
he always had this look on his face.

146
00:09:35,604 --> 00:09:37,734
He wouldn't talk to anyone, either.

147
00:09:38,174 --> 00:09:40,664
Not even to you?

148
00:09:41,114 --> 00:09:44,074
No. He was always alone.

149
00:09:47,784 --> 00:09:50,084
We tried introducing him to the children.

150
00:09:50,584 --> 00:09:53,574
At first they were interested in him.

151
00:09:54,024 --> 00:09:59,554
But he never paid attention to anyone,
so they stopped coming near him.

152
00:10:05,164 --> 00:10:07,964
He didn't seem to have any
friends at school, either.

153
00:10:08,904 --> 00:10:15,334
He was the type that just wouldn't let anyone
close to him, so perhaps it couldn't be helped.

154
00:10:17,684 --> 00:10:19,144
Hello.

155
00:10:23,414 --> 00:10:25,984
You're supposed to say, "I'm home"!

156
00:10:25,984 --> 00:10:28,224
I don't like Fujimoto.

157
00:10:28,224 --> 00:10:29,694
Me neither!

158
00:10:31,894 --> 00:10:33,954
Bye-bye Sayaka.

159
00:10:34,194 --> 00:10:36,394
Bye. See you tomorrow.

160
00:10:52,984 --> 00:10:56,914
Fujimoto, you like the organ?

161
00:10:59,754 --> 00:11:00,984
Fujimoto?!

162
00:11:11,404 --> 00:11:12,994
Sayaka!

163
00:11:13,734 --> 00:11:16,464
See you tomorrow!

164
00:11:41,164 --> 00:11:42,854
Fujimoto...

165
00:12:03,884 --> 00:12:05,354
Free Sampling Campaign
New Product!

166
00:12:05,354 --> 00:12:05,854
Free Sampling Campaign
New Product!
Anybody like some ice cold beer?

167
00:12:05,854 --> 00:12:07,324
Anybody like some ice cold beer?

168
00:12:07,854 --> 00:12:10,224
We're giving away free samples.

169
00:12:11,024 --> 00:12:12,264
Can I have one?

170
00:12:12,264 --> 00:12:13,524
Here you go.

171
00:12:13,624 --> 00:12:15,564
Would you like some really good beer?

172
00:12:15,564 --> 00:12:17,624
We're presently conducting a campaign.

173
00:12:17,734 --> 00:12:18,724
Um...

174
00:12:18,864 --> 00:12:20,924
Is this free?

175
00:12:21,174 --> 00:12:23,634
Y-Yes. It's a new product.

176
00:12:23,734 --> 00:12:25,264
Please try some.

177
00:12:26,744 --> 00:12:30,944
Thank you very much.
Shuichiro will be so happy.

178
00:12:40,324 --> 00:12:45,484
It was a beautiful summer day like today.

179
00:12:46,764 --> 00:12:48,464
It's my turn next.

180
00:12:48,464 --> 00:12:50,334
No it isn't. It's my turn!

181
00:12:50,334 --> 00:12:52,264
Kuri, you already went.

182
00:12:52,834 --> 00:12:55,304
Come on now, no fighting.
Everybody wait your turn.

183
00:12:55,504 --> 00:12:56,734
Yes ma'am,

184
00:12:57,704 --> 00:12:59,774
Do you think they'll blossom soon?

185
00:12:59,774 --> 00:13:00,944
Why sure.

186
00:13:00,944 --> 00:13:05,384
I'm sure they'll blossom beautifully, because
you all have taken such good care of them.

187
00:13:05,444 --> 00:13:06,674
Really?!

188
00:13:06,844 --> 00:13:07,984
Really.

189
00:13:07,984 --> 00:13:09,174
Yeah!

190
00:13:09,254 --> 00:13:12,684
Well then everybody. Tidy up before you play.

191
00:13:12,884 --> 00:13:14,444
Yes ma'am!

192
00:13:27,604 --> 00:13:28,794
Hello.

193
00:13:38,314 --> 00:13:39,944
Tomo, are you all right?

194
00:13:40,314 --> 00:13:42,514
You know what? A ball came flying.

195
00:13:42,514 --> 00:13:44,814
Tomo got surprised and fell over.

196
00:13:47,084 --> 00:13:48,154
Sayaka!

197
00:13:48,154 --> 00:13:51,024
Tomo, did you get hurt? Are you okay?

198
00:13:56,994 --> 00:13:58,534
Why did you push me?

199
00:13:58,534 --> 00:14:00,004
Sorry man.

200
00:14:00,004 --> 00:14:01,934
I didn't think you'd really fall.

201
00:14:01,934 --> 00:14:05,274
This isn't funny. I'm all covered in dirt.

202
00:14:05,274 --> 00:14:07,614
Never mind. Hurry up and go find the ball.

203
00:14:07,614 --> 00:14:09,544
It's all because of your lousy pass.

204
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:11,704
I know.

205
00:14:11,914 --> 00:14:13,944
Darn! It won't come off.

206
00:14:13,944 --> 00:14:16,114
Why is it so wet here?

207
00:14:16,814 --> 00:14:18,084
Hey!

208
00:14:18,184 --> 00:14:20,084
What are you guys doing?!

209
00:14:20,384 --> 00:14:23,654
Oh, well... our ball came in and uh...

210
00:14:23,654 --> 00:14:25,064
Do you realize how dangerous that is?!

211
00:14:25,064 --> 00:14:26,994
You almost hit this child!

212
00:14:27,564 --> 00:14:29,194
But it didn't hit her, did it?

213
00:14:29,194 --> 00:14:30,754
What are you so upset about?

214
00:14:30,934 --> 00:14:32,594
And get out of the garden, now!

215
00:14:32,704 --> 00:14:33,604
Huh?

216
00:14:33,604 --> 00:14:38,564
We planted these sunflowers together and
have been taking great care of them!

217
00:14:39,044 --> 00:14:41,804
We've been looking forward to seeing them
blossom, very soon!

218
00:14:49,414 --> 00:14:50,644
Here's your ball!

219
00:14:51,484 --> 00:14:54,454
I want you to apologize to this girl,
and all the children. Then leave!

220
00:15:07,104 --> 00:15:09,094
Um. That was our fault.

221
00:15:09,334 --> 00:15:10,604
Sorry about that.

222
00:15:12,444 --> 00:15:14,704
Your trap was too big.

223
00:15:14,874 --> 00:15:18,404
Then you shouldn't have passed it way out
there. How do you expect me to reach it?

224
00:15:25,684 --> 00:15:26,984
Sayaka.

225
00:15:28,624 --> 00:15:30,214
The sunflower...

226
00:15:36,764 --> 00:15:38,024
It'll be okay.

227
00:15:38,764 --> 00:15:41,464
It just got hurt a little.

228
00:15:46,104 --> 00:15:48,304
We hold it up like this...

229
00:15:49,144 --> 00:15:52,474
Water it every day and it'll bloom for sure.

230
00:15:52,744 --> 00:15:53,814
Really?

231
00:15:53,814 --> 00:15:54,804
Yes.

232
00:16:11,664 --> 00:16:16,634
I see white, I see white

233
00:16:16,634 --> 00:16:21,514
Chasing clouds as they drift away

234
00:16:21,514 --> 00:16:26,374
Let's all run, let's all run

235
00:16:26,614 --> 00:16:31,174
Me and my friends, 'cause we love to play

236
00:16:31,754 --> 00:16:36,494
When we get to the top of the hill

237
00:16:36,494 --> 00:16:40,984
We can see everything, what a thrill

238
00:16:41,594 --> 00:16:46,054
Let's go look, let's go look

239
00:16:46,434 --> 00:16:51,164
Let's find wonderful things today

240
00:16:55,614 --> 00:16:59,714
Are you aware that Fujimoto has a lot of jobs?

241
00:16:59,714 --> 00:17:01,084
Yes, I do.

242
00:17:01,084 --> 00:17:06,584
He delivers pizzas, does bicycle-courier,
delivers newspapers, and a whole lot more.

243
00:17:06,584 --> 00:17:08,054
That many?

244
00:17:08,194 --> 00:17:13,684
Yes. He's helping in every way he can
to pay back kindergarten loans.

245
00:17:15,934 --> 00:17:17,764
He's doing it for the kindergarten?

246
00:17:18,304 --> 00:17:21,804
That's right. And he seems to be
studying until very late every night.

247
00:17:21,804 --> 00:17:24,434
He says he wants to become a lawyer.

248
00:17:24,974 --> 00:17:28,414
I'm worried he's going to make himself sick.

249
00:17:43,254 --> 00:17:45,954
Soft, and a nice scent!

250
00:17:47,164 --> 00:17:48,784
It's the smell of the sun.

251
00:17:48,934 --> 00:17:50,394
The sun?

252
00:17:50,394 --> 00:17:51,364
That's right.

253
00:17:51,364 --> 00:17:54,564
When you hang futons out,
they smell like the sun.

254
00:17:55,374 --> 00:17:58,604
Well, that's what my father told me anyway.

255
00:18:00,504 --> 00:18:05,004
So tomorrow, everybody gets
to take a nap with the sun.

256
00:18:07,644 --> 00:18:08,914
That's right.

257
00:18:09,084 --> 00:18:11,184
Did I say something funny?

258
00:18:11,184 --> 00:18:14,154
No. Not at all. It's wonderful, isn't it?

259
00:18:14,154 --> 00:18:16,784
Yes. I'm looking forward to tomorrow.

260
00:18:17,224 --> 00:18:19,124
Shall we bring them in, then?

261
00:18:19,224 --> 00:18:20,324
Yes!

262
00:18:25,464 --> 00:18:27,934
Thank you for coming today.
Be careful on your way home.

263
00:18:28,074 --> 00:18:30,034
Yes. See you tomorrow.

264
00:18:34,074 --> 00:18:35,704
The sun...

265
00:18:40,914 --> 00:18:42,284
It's Fujimoto!

266
00:18:42,414 --> 00:18:43,754
Welcome home!

267
00:18:43,754 --> 00:18:45,654
Hey, will you play the organ again?

268
00:18:45,754 --> 00:18:47,444
Yeah, play it for us, please.

269
00:18:48,554 --> 00:18:50,294
Hey! It's Fujimoto!

270
00:18:50,294 --> 00:18:51,324
Yeah, it is!

271
00:18:51,324 --> 00:18:52,794
Welcome home!

272
00:18:56,694 --> 00:18:58,064
Hello.

273
00:19:01,204 --> 00:19:04,464
I uh... I...

274
00:19:06,244 --> 00:19:07,464
I'm home!

275
00:19:07,874 --> 00:19:10,444
Come on, Fujimoto, the organ, the organ.

276
00:19:10,444 --> 00:19:11,974
Hurry, hurry...

277
00:19:15,784 --> 00:19:20,274
I see red, I see red

278
00:19:20,484 --> 00:19:24,784
Sunset color, pretty as a poem

279
00:19:25,264 --> 00:19:30,134
Let us walk, let us walk

280
00:19:30,134 --> 00:19:34,434
It's that time of day, no time to roam

281
00:19:35,004 --> 00:19:39,574
If tomorrow we see the sun

282
00:19:39,574 --> 00:19:43,904
Let's meet again for play and fun

283
00:19:45,744 --> 00:19:50,984
Bye for now, bye for now

284
00:19:51,084 --> 00:19:55,784
It's time to go, yes, there is your home

285
00:19:57,194 --> 00:20:00,024
See that?! There's no increase
in the number of kompeito!

286
00:20:00,364 --> 00:20:07,024
Uhh... but, but, I wanted to take out the futons.
I wanted to be of help to the kindergarten.

287
00:20:07,204 --> 00:20:09,734
Not just the futons, you hung me out there too.

288
00:20:09,734 --> 00:20:11,394
I'm sorry.

289
00:20:11,604 --> 00:20:13,704
Kobato. Ioryogi-san.

290
00:20:15,314 --> 00:20:17,004
I thought it might be you.

291
00:20:18,784 --> 00:20:22,774
Perfect timing. I was about to
bring this over to you.

292
00:20:25,654 --> 00:20:28,414
I-Is this allowed?!

293
00:20:28,754 --> 00:20:33,214
Yes. I have one in the fridge for Shuichiro.

294
00:20:33,464 --> 00:20:34,824
Well then thank you.

295
00:20:34,964 --> 00:20:37,364
Wasn't that nice, Ioryogi-san?

296
00:20:37,364 --> 00:20:39,354
Okay, bottoms up!

297
00:20:39,704 --> 00:20:45,334
No wait. I'm going to fight the urge now
and enjoy it before I go to bed!

298
00:20:47,204 --> 00:20:52,974
Kohaku, you're always properly watering the
trees in your garden. I'm impressed.

299
00:20:53,414 --> 00:20:57,744
It's about all I can do for Shuichiro.

300
00:20:58,324 --> 00:21:02,844
But every little bit I can do for
him makes me feel good.

301
00:21:03,024 --> 00:21:07,184
I'm happy too, whenever I'm able
to help Yomogi Kindergarten.

302
00:21:07,324 --> 00:21:12,194
Yes. Happiness is being able to
help those who are dear to you.

303
00:21:13,734 --> 00:21:15,434
Those who are dear.

304
00:21:19,574 --> 00:21:24,634
Yomogi Kindergarten is very
dear to Fujimoto, isn't it?

305
00:21:25,014 --> 00:21:29,844
I should think so, seeing the number
of jobs he does for them.

306
00:21:30,884 --> 00:21:32,184
To me too.

307
00:21:32,754 --> 00:21:34,154
I feel...

308
00:21:34,154 --> 00:21:35,024
Huh?

309
00:21:35,124 --> 00:21:39,354
I feel that Yomogi Kindergarten
is very dear to me.

310
00:21:39,764 --> 00:21:44,064
I want to be able to help Ms. Sayaka
and the others as much as I can!

311
00:21:45,634 --> 00:21:48,034
Kobato is ready!

312
00:21:48,234 --> 00:21:52,104
Why do I get the feeling we're heading
in the wrong direction again?

313
00:22:18,564 --> 00:22:20,554
Hello Kobato.

314
00:22:20,734 --> 00:22:23,104
Welcome home.

315
00:22:23,104 --> 00:22:24,594
Hi, I'm back.

316
00:22:24,744 --> 00:22:26,264
Oh! Fujimoto!

317
00:22:26,344 --> 00:22:29,274
You were a very cute child!

318
00:22:30,114 --> 00:22:35,774
And, and when you were small, you had trouble
reaching the pedals of the organ, right?!

319
00:22:36,854 --> 00:22:38,784
How do you know that stuff?!

320
00:22:38,984 --> 00:22:42,444
Ms. Sayaka showed me pictures of you today!

321
00:22:42,594 --> 00:22:43,924
I wanna see them!

322
00:22:43,924 --> 00:22:44,864
Me too!

323
00:22:44,864 --> 00:22:46,324
I'd like to see them too.

324
00:22:46,324 --> 00:22:47,564
Tiny Fujimoto!

325
00:22:47,564 --> 00:22:48,234
Not you too, Ms. Chisato!

326
00:22:48,234 --> 00:22:48,734
He's tiny and cute, but has a
big pout on his face.
Not you too, Ms. Chisato!

327
00:22:48,734 --> 00:22:50,794
He's tiny and cute, but has a
big pout on his face.

328
00:22:50,794 --> 00:22:51,934
Don't say another word!

329
00:22:51,934 --> 00:22:53,134
Tell us more!

330
00:22:53,134 --> 00:22:55,174
Um... What shall I do now?

331
00:22:55,174 --> 00:22:58,074
Then later, when he's not around.

332
00:23:01,344 --> 00:23:08,974
Hito wa mina tonde mitai no ni

333
00:23:10,154 --> 00:23:16,254
Juuryoku ni damasareterunda

334
00:23:16,524 --> 00:23:24,364
Dare mo honto wa toberunda yo

335
00:23:26,604 --> 00:23:32,934
Ano ko ga anna ni kanashisou na no wa

336
00:23:33,974 --> 00:23:36,844
Jibun no kage wo

337
00:23:36,844 --> 00:23:43,974
Dokoka ni wasurete kichatta kara kamo

338
00:23:44,154 --> 00:23:46,674
Sore nara

339
00:23:46,854 --> 00:23:50,954
"Arigatou," tte kimi ni ietara

340
00:23:50,954 --> 00:23:54,834
"Arigatou," tte kimi ga waraeba

341
00:23:54,834 --> 00:24:02,164
Ittari kitari ureshiku naru

342
00:24:02,704 --> 00:24:06,934
Kimi ga shiawase ni naru

343
00:24:07,244 --> 00:24:11,484
Shinpai nante iranai yo

344
00:24:11,484 --> 00:24:15,574
Issho ni iru kara

345
00:24:17,354 --> 00:24:23,294
Ureshikuttemo namida ga deru nante

346
00:24:23,294 --> 00:24:26,094
Fushigi da

347
00:24:26,094 --> 00:24:29,034
Next episode
...Detective Kobato Hanato.
Fushigi da

348
00:24:29,034 --> 00:24:30,724
Next episode
...Detective Kobato Hanato.

